{
  "$comment": "eApps R6 (VAPP-222, docs/spec/apps.md §3.3/§3.4): a kind's state machine on ONE enum field, `records.<kind>.transitions: {field, from: {state: [next…]}, initial?: [state…], who?: {\"a->b\" | state: level}}`. TS reference src/host/record-transitions.ts, Rust twin eui-core `host::record_transitions`, the Swift and Compose SDKs over the FFI (`transition_refusal_json`, `transitions_from_json`, `validate_record_transitions_json`); the Exponential server enforces it in the records service (every create, patch and batch write). Inputs hand-written, `expected` filled by scripts/generate-host.ts. VALIDATE (`validateCases`: validateRecordTransitions(kind, at, kindName), at = `/records/<kindName>`): issues under `<at>/transitions`: an unknown key; `field` a declared string field with an `enum` (its values are the STATES); every `from` key, every next state and every `initial` entry a state; `initial` a non-empty list; a `who` key is a declared edge `a->b` or a state (`b` = every edge into it); its level `member`, `author`, `owners` or `role:<field>` where `<field>` is a `member` ref of the kind (R5 `refs`); a kind with transitions declares no field or computed field `transitions` (its rows carry the next states there). Keys in code-unit order. REFUSAL (`refusalCases`: transitionRefusal(kindTransitions(kind), before, after, viewer, row)): `before` = the stored data (null = a create), `after` = the data as it would be stored (an update = the patch merged), `viewer` = {id, role}, `row` = the record's ownership (the author = `authorId ?? createdBy`). A state is a non-empty string at `field` (else none). Unchanged = null (any write that does not move the state passes). No state before (a create, or a record without one): the new state is none or an INITIAL state (`initial`, else every `from` state no edge enters, else every `from` state; code-unit order) else BAD_REQUEST `<field>: a new record starts in <initial, comma-separated>`. A cleared state or an edge `from[a]` does not list = BAD_REQUEST `<field>: <a> → <b|(none)> is not a declared transition`. Then the edge's level (`who[\"a->b\"]`, else `who[b]`, else member): member = anyone; a team owner takes every edge; `owners` = FORBIDDEN `Only team owners can move <field> to <b>`; `author` = the record's author else FORBIDDEN `Only the record's author or a team owner can move <field> to <b>`; `role:<f>` = the member `before[f]` names (before the write: a mover never names themselves in the same write) else FORBIDDEN `Only the record's <f> or a team owner can move <field> to <b>`; an unknown level = FORBIDDEN `Nobody can move <field> to <b>`. FROM (`fromCases`: transitionsFrom(kindTransitions(kind), record, viewer?, row)): the next states of the record's state in the declared order (no state = the initial states), only those the viewer may take when a viewer is given; no transitions = []. The records query (records-query.json VAPP-222 cases) writes them into every row of the kind as `transitions` for the context's viewer (`me` + `role`).",
  "kind": {
    "schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "title": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "status": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "requested",
            "approved",
            "rejected",
            "paid"
          ]
        },
        "approver": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "amount": {
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "title"
      ]
    },
    "refs": {
      "approver": "member"
    },
    "transitions": {
      "field": "status",
      "initial": [
        "requested"
      ],
      "from": {
        "requested": [
          "approved",
          "rejected"
        ],
        "approved": [
          "paid"
        ],
        "rejected": [
          "requested"
        ]
      },
      "who": {
        "requested->approved": "role:approver",
        "requested->rejected": "role:approver",
        "paid": "owners",
        "rejected->requested": "author"
      }
    }
  },
